# What the deploy is allowed to contain.
#
# The output directory is the repo root (see vercel.json), so every source
# file, test fixture screenshot and doc would otherwise be published alongside
# the app and served at its own URL. An allowlist rather than a list of
# exclusions, in the form Vercel documents: a directory added later should have
# to be let in deliberately, not be published because nobody remembered to name
# it here.
#
# `static/` is the whole app — the page, its stylesheet, the built bundle, the
# icons, the manifest, the service worker, the OpenCV build and the digit
# exemplars — and vercel.json is what maps four of those onto root URLs.
#
# This is tidiness and deploy size, not secrecy. The repo is public and holds
# no secrets, which is just as well: nothing here is *verified* by a test, and
# it is the one piece of the deploy that only the deploy can prove.
/*
!/static
!/vercel.json
